[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Alternative Web Automation Tools: Playwright and Cypress"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"While Selenium has long been the industry standard for web automation testing, modern alternatives like Playwright and Cypress have revolutionized the testing landscape. They offer faster execution, better developer experience, and native handling of modern web application complexities."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Understanding Playwright"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Developed by Microsoft, Playwright is an open-source end-to-end testing framework. It enables reliable web automation across all modern rendering engines including Chromium, WebKit, and Firefox using a single API."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Cross-browser support: Test on Chromium, Firefox, and Safari with real mobile emulation."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Auto-waiting: Playwright automatically waits for elements to be actionable before performing actions, reducing flaky tests."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Network interception: Built-in capability to stub and mock network requests and responses easily."},{"order":8,"type":"code","text":"const { test, expect } = require('@playwright/test');

test('basic test', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('https://example.com');
  const title = await page.title();
  expect(title).toBe('Example Domain');
});"},{"order":9,"type":"subheading","text":"Understanding Cypress"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"Cypress is a front-end automated testing tool built for the modern web. Unlike tools that operate outside the browser, Cypress operates directly inside the browser loop, giving it native access to DOM elements and application state."},{"order":11,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Time travel: Cypress takes snapshots of your application as your tests run, allowing you to hover over commands to see what happened at each step."},{"order":12,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Real-time reloads: Automatically reloads your tests as you make changes to your test files."},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Automatic waiting: Automatically waits for commands and assertions before moving on."},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"describe('My First Test', () => {
  it('Visits the kitchen sink', () => {
    cy.visit('https://example.cypress.io');
    cy.contains('type').click();
    cy.url().should('include', '/commands/actions');
  });
});"},{"order":15,"type":"subheading","text":"Choosing Between Playwright and Cypress"},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Choose Playwright if you need multi-tab support, native mobile web testing, parallel execution across different browser engines, or language support beyond JavaScript/TypeScript (Python, C#, Java)."},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Choose Cypress if you are working exclusively in a JavaScript/TypeScript ecosystem, prefer an interactive debugging GUI, and want an out-of-the-box solution with minimal setup."}]
